Bugfix: Open the user menu with the keyboard

The user menu in the header of the signed-in application - Settings, Users,
Log out - could only be opened with a mouse. The toggle was reachable with
the Tab key and showed a focus ring, but pressing Enter or Space had no
effect, so keyboard users could not reach the log out entry or their personal
settings at all. The toggle was a div carrying role="link", and a div does
not turn a key press into a click the way a real control does.

The toggle is now a native button. Enter and Space open and close the menu,
the focus ring is unchanged, and the header looks exactly as before: every
measured position and size of the toggle, the user name and the surrounding
container is identical, with and without a profile picture.

WCAG 2.1 AA, SC 2.1.1
